# VS Code REST Client examples. Preserve its cookie jar.
# Re-run the csrf request before EVERY POST/PATCH, including after login/logout/guest.
# Use your own credentials and IDs. No default accounts or passwords are supplied.
@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:9090/api
@providerId = REPLACE_FROM_APPROVED_APPLICATION
@patientId = REPLACE_FROM_GUEST_RESPONSE
@bookingId = REPLACE_FROM_BOOKING_RESPONSE
@date = REPLACE_WITH_TOMORROW_YYYY-MM-DD

### Fetch a fresh session-bound CSRF token
# @name csrf
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/csrf

### Current authenticated identity
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/session

### Guest patient entry (no login)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/guest
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf.response.body.$.token}}

{"language":"en"}

### Save guest contact details before booking
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/patients/{{patientId}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf.response.body.$.token}}

{"name":"Patient name","phone":"9876543210","village":"rama"}

### Public approved/activated providers
GET {{baseUrl}}/providers

### Real slot availability
GET {{baseUrl}}/providers/{{providerId}}/slots?date={{date}}

### Request appointment as current guest
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf.response.body.$.token}}

{"pid":"{{providerId}}","date":"{{date}}","time":"10:00","reason":"Consultation"}

### Own appointment records
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings

### Use the application login UI or Postman collection to establish a provider session.
### Accept is only allowed for the currently signed-in assigned provider.
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}/accept
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf.response.body.$.token}}

{}

### Cancellation requires the original guest or assigned provider session
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf.response.body.$.token}}

{}
